---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GameGrid from '../components/GameGrid.astro';
import CompactGameGrid from '../components/CompactGameGrid.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import CategoryLinks from '../components/CategoryLinks.astro';
import { games, categoryGames, canonical, gamePath, itemListSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/catalog.mjs';
const sledGames = categoryGames('sledding-games');
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What are the best free sled games to play online?',
    a: 'Our current sledding choices are Sled Rider and Snow Rider 2. Both feature downhill survival runs and gift collecting. Start with Sled Rider for its detailed beginner walkthrough, or choose Snow Rider 2 for the Snow Rider 3D release identified on its game page.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to download anything to play sled games?',
    a: 'No app installation is needed. Open a game card to visit its player page, keep JavaScript enabled, and allow the game to load. If a player stays stuck, its Reload button lets you try again without leaving the page.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I play sled games on a phone?',
    a: 'Support varies by game. Snow Rider 2 is listed as compatible with iOS and Android browsers in its official catalog. Check the player for touch controls before starting, and use landscape orientation if that makes the course easier to see.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between a sled game and a snowboard game?',
    a: 'A sled game puts you on a sled or sleigh; a snowboard game puts a rider on a board. Similar snowy scenery does not mean identical rules: snowboard games here include both survival challenges and finish-line courses. Browse the Snowboard Games category to compare those options.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are these sled games free?',
    a: 'Yes. There is no Sled Games access fee or account requirement. Games load through third-party publishing platforms, which may show advertisements and set their own in-game terms. The game pages include controls and guides alongside the free browser players.',
  },
];
---
<Layout snowfall title="Sled Games - Play Free Sledding Games Online" description="Play free sled games in your web browser. Ride a sled down snowy slopes, then explore our snowboard, ski, and Christmas game pages." schema={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Sled Games', url: canonical('/') }, itemListSchema(sledGames, 'Sled Games'), faqSchema(faqs)]}>
  <section class="page-intro hub-intro">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">PICK YOUR NEXT RUN</span><h1>Sled Games</h1><p>Choose a downhill sledding run, compare the controls, and open a game when you're ready. Start with the sled games below, or use Quick Start to jump into a game.</p></div>
    {sledGames.length > 0 && <a class="button" data-random-game href={gamePath(sledGames[0].slug)}>Quick Start <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>}
  </section>
  <section class="featured-games" aria-labelledby="sled-games-collection">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><h2 id="sled-games-collection">Choose your sled game</h2><p>Downhill runs, each with its own player and guide.</p></div></div>
    <GameGrid games={sledGames} eager />
  </section>
  <CategoryLinks />
  <article class="content-section hub-guide prose" aria-label="Choosing sled games">
    <section aria-labelledby="what-are-sled-games">
      <h2 id="what-are-sled-games">What are sled games?</h2>
      <p>Sled games put you on a sled or sleigh moving across snow, with the route in front of you setting the challenge. In the downhill games featured here, the sled advances automatically; you choose where to steer, when to jump, and whether a collectible is worth leaving a clear line. A run continues until a collision or fall ends it.</p>
      <p>This page focuses on sledding. Sled Rider and Snow Rider 2 are the current choices, rather than a list of every winter sport. The Snow Rider 2 page explains that its player runs Snow Rider 3D, so you can check which release you are opening before starting.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="pick-a-sled-game">
      <h2 id="pick-a-sled-game">How to pick a sled game</h2>
      <h3>Endless runners vs level-based games</h3>
      <p>The first choice is the kind of goal you want. An endless runner asks how long you can keep a run alive, while a level-based game gives you a course or stage to complete. Both sled games in this collection are endless runs. Choose them for repeated attempts at distance and gift collecting, rather than expecting a finish line or fixed levels.</p>
      <p>If finishing marked courses matters more to you, use the category links above. Ski King offers ski courses, and SnowBoard Game has a finish-line objective. Those are different sports, so they live in their own categories and the <a href="/games/">All Winter Games</a> directory.</p>
      <h3>Keyboard or touch controls</h3>
      <p>Check your device before choosing a game. A keyboard gives you separate inputs for steering and jumping; each detail page lists the keys used by that game. Read those labels instead of assuming that every sledding game shares the same layout.</p>
      <p>On a phone, look for the controls visible inside the player. A mobile compatibility listing does not mean the keyboard instructions describe touch input. If the controls are missing or awkward to use, try a keyboard device or look through the other categories for a game with documented touch controls.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="sled-games-beginners">
      <h2 id="sled-games-beginners">Sled games for beginners</h2>
      <p>For a first session, choose one game and read its controls table before pressing play. <a href={gamePath('sled-rider')}>Sled Rider</a> is a useful starting point if you want a guide that breaks a run into starting, steering, jumping, collecting, and retrying. Its game page has the complete walkthrough.</p>
      <p>Give your first few attempts one goal: stay on open snow. Saving every present can pull you into a turn you have not prepared for. Once steering feels predictable, add gift collecting to your next attempt. Compare your own decisions across runs instead of looking for a universal easiest game.</p>
      <p>When trying another sledding game, keep the same practice goal for a few attempts. That makes differences in timing and movement easier to notice. If a run ends quickly, decide whether you turned late, chose a blocked landing, or chased a risky gift before restarting.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <section class="content-section home-collection" aria-labelledby="every-winter-game">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="every-winter-game">Browse every winter game</h2>
        <p>All {games.length} games on Sled Games, in one place. Open any card to play, or use the full directory for details and guides.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <CompactGameGrid games={games} />
    <p class="collection-more"><a class="text-link" href="/games/">See the full winter collection</a></p>
  </section>
  <Faq faqs={faqs} />
  <section class="editorial-note"><h2>Find your next winter game</h2><p>Pick a sled game from the collection above, or browse our <a href="/snowboard-games/">snowboard</a>, <a href="/ski-games/">ski</a>, and <a href="/christmas-games/">Christmas game</a> categories for something different. Visit the <a href="/games/">full winter collection</a> to see every game in one place.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">About Sled Games →</a></section>
  <script is:inline>
  {
    const randomStart = document.querySelector('[data-random-game]');
    randomStart?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const choices = document.querySelectorAll('.featured-games .game-card');
      const choice = choices[Math.floor(Math.random() * choices.length)];
      if (choice) randomStart.href = choice.href;
    });
  }
  </script>
</Layout>
